---
// Privacy policy (docs/LAUNCH-FLOW.md §3 and §6). Plain language, and short because we collect
// so little. Have it reviewed by an attorney who does children's privacy before ads run.
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '@lib/url';
const updated = 'November 10, 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Lostman’s River collects, and what it never does.">
  <article class="wrap section legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Short version: we keep the email address of the grown-up who buys the Experience, and an anonymous record of which missions are done. We never ask a child for anything, and there are no ads or trackers in the Experience.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>Lostman’s River (lostmansriver.com) is published by McKillop Creative, LLC, home of the novel <em>Escape to Lostman’s River</em> by Linda and John McKillop. Questions: <a href="mailto:help@lostmansriver.com">help@lostmansriver.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>When you buy the Experience:</strong> your email address, from checkout, so we can send your reader’s link and send it again if you lose it. Payment is handled by Stripe; we never see or store card details.</li>
      <li><strong>If you ask for the holiday promo code:</strong> your email address, the date, and which ad or link brought you (a campaign name, never anything about you), so we can send the code and one reminder before Christmas. Only grown-ups may ask. Every email has a one-click way off the list, and we delete the list in January except for anyone who buys.</li>
      <li><strong>Your purchase link:</strong> a random code that unlocks the Experience. It is not tied to your child’s name or anything about them.</li>
      <li><strong>Progress:</strong> which missions and field missions are done (and the date a grown-up signed each field mission off), which badges are earned, and the date the summer started, saved under that random code so the summer picks up on any device.</li>
      <li><strong>Counts of what happens on the site:</strong> for example, how many people played Chapter 1 or finished Mission 6. These are tallies with no identifier attached: no name, email, IP address or device ID is stored with them. Page views are counted by Cloudflare Web Analytics, which does not use cookies.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we never collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Nothing from children. The Experience never asks a reader for their name, email, age, photo, location or anything they type. The name written on the printable license stays on that device and is never sent to us.</li>
      <li>No cookies for tracking, no advertising trackers, and no third-party ad pixels on any page a reader uses: the app, chapters, missions, games and license.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>If you reach our landing page from an online ad, that page may tell the ad platform (Meta) that the visit happened and what you did on it: how far you scrolled, whether you played the sample or tapped a link, and whether you began a purchase, so we can see which ads work. This happens only on that page, which is written for grown-ups, and only for visits that came from an ad click.</p>
    <p>If you arrive from a Meta (Facebook or Instagram) ad, your browser remembers that ad click for 7 days. If you then buy, our server tells Meta that a purchase happened: the price, the ad click, and your email address in scrambled (hashed) form, which is how Meta matches a sale to an ad without being sent the address itself. When you tap Buy after arriving from a Meta ad, our server also tells Meta that a checkout started: the price, the ad click, and your device’s IP address and browser type, which is how Meta matches it to the ad. No email or name is sent then. Purchases and checkouts that did not start from a Meta ad are not reported. Nothing about your child is ever sent. It never happens on any page a reader uses.</p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>Only the services that run the site: Stripe (payment), Cloudflare (hosting, email delivery, storage and the anonymous counts) and GitHub (hosting the public pages), plus Meta only as described under Advertising. We do not sell or rent any information, and we do not share it for anyone else’s marketing.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Your email and the progress record are kept while the Experience is yours to use, so the link keeps working. Email us and we will delete both; the link then stops working.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The Experience is made for readers about 10 to 15, bought by a parent or guardian. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 13, and the Experience has no place to enter any: no accounts, no sign-in, no forms, no messages, no photos. A child’s use involves no personal data beyond the anonymous progress record described above, which is tied to the purchase code, not to the child. The purchase email belongs to the grown-up who bought it. If you believe a child has sent us personal information, email us and we will delete it.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete what we hold about you at any time: <a href="mailto:help@lostmansriver.com">help@lostmansriver.com</a>. If we change this policy we will update the date at the top, and tell buyers by email if the change matters.</p>

    <p class="small"><a href={url('/terms/')}>Terms</a> · <a href={url('/')}>Home</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>

